Why: Typed-only /pfd, paths fixed for the flattened layout, version history cut, Codex typed-only.

Problem: upstream is a plugin: skills/pfd plus repo-level framework/, corpus/, commands/ and scripts/.
upstreams.toml flattens them into one skill dir, which breaks its plugin-root-relative paths. Its
long description triggers on any design or copy task and loads every session, and the SKILL.md
carries a version history the agent reads on every use.

Change: a one-line description and `disable-model-invocation: true`; the path-conventions line says
every path is relative to this skill's dir; the Version History section is deleted;
agents/openai.yaml makes it typed-only in Codex.

Keep when rebasing: the CC BY-SA 4.0 license and NOTICE (copied by upstreams.toml). Share-alike
applies to this patch.

Reapply: frontmatter, the path-conventions line, delete the version history, re-add openai.yaml. If
upstream adds top-level dirs that SKILL.md references, add them to `paths` in upstreams.toml.

